  "id": "Compound::DB00509 - Gene::53919",
  "verbalization": "Dextrothyroxine is likely to interact with Slco1c1 through a series of molecular and cellular mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Dextrothyroxine binds to Slco4a1, which is involved in the transport of organic anions, and further participates in thyroid hormone transmembrane transporter activity, as well as modified amino acid transmembrane transporter activity. These pathways are all associated with Slco1c1, indicating a potential functional link between Dextrothyroxine and Slco1c1. The binding of Dextrothyroxine to Slco4a1 may influence the activity of Slco1c1, potentially modulating its role in transporting thyroid hormones or other molecules across cellular membranes. The overlapping pathways suggest that Dextrothyroxine may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving Slco4a1 and Slco1c1, highlighting a possible regulatory or functional relationship between these entities.",
